1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,917
A concrete candidate counterexample to the Jacobian Conjecture was reported.

2
00:00:04,917 --> 00:00:08,345
But a reported formula is not yet a verified theorem.

3
00:00:08,345 --> 00:00:15,979
Before repeating the headline, we need an exact reconstruction, explicit witnesses, and an inspectable trust boundary.

4
00:00:16,779 --> 00:00:20,938
Breaking Math Verification is a reusable workflow for that moment.

5
00:00:20,938 --> 00:00:22,828
Start with the reported claim.

6
00:00:22,828 --> 00:00:25,159
Transcribe its objects independently.

7
00:00:25,159 --> 00:00:30,074
Prove symbolic identities, check finite witnesses, and derive the consequence.

8
00:00:30,074 --> 00:00:35,808
Then publish a small Lean certificate and its axioms, keeping provenance and scope visible.

9
00:00:36,608 --> 00:00:43,371
For this case study, I independently transcribed the reported three-dimensional polynomial map into Lean.

10
00:00:43,371 --> 00:00:45,432
Its coordinates are P, Q, and R.

11
00:00:45,432 --> 00:00:50,005
Their exact formulas remain visible and traceable in the source module.

12
00:00:50,805 --> 00:00:59,406
Lean differentiates the multivariable polynomials symbolically and proves that the original formal Jacobian determinant is minus two.

13
00:00:59,406 --> 00:01:07,232
Multiplying the first output coordinate by minus one half gives a normalized map whose formal determinant is exactly one.

14
00:01:08,032 --> 00:01:09,985
The global witness is finite.

15
00:01:09,985 --> 00:01:14,631
Lean checks three pairwise-distinct inputs: p zero, p one, and p two.

16
00:01:14,631 --> 00:01:18,065
All map to the same target: one eighth, zero, zero.

17
00:01:18,065 --> 00:01:23,115
These are exact complex-coordinate equalities, with no numerical tolerance.

18
00:01:23,915 --> 00:01:27,798
Two distinct inputs with one output refute injectivity.

19
00:01:27,798 --> 00:01:34,858
DkMath packages that logic as a reusable Collision Certificate, independent of Jacobian polynomials.

20
00:01:34,858 --> 00:01:42,624
The adapter supplies p zero and p one; generic consequences prove non-injectivity and rule out a left inverse.

21
00:01:43,424 --> 00:01:45,802
These are compiled Lean declarations.

22
00:01:45,802 --> 00:01:50,430
The normalized certificate combines determinant one and non-injectivity.

23
00:01:50,430 --> 00:01:54,287
The three-point theorem records distinctness and evaluation.

24
00:01:54,287 --> 00:02:03,157
The audit reports propext, Classical choice, and Quot sound for the Jacobian certificate; the generic collision consequence has no axioms.

25
00:02:03,957 --> 00:02:09,250
GPT five point six helped analyze the mathematics and review theorem boundaries.

26
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:13,087
Codex implemented the Lean modules and ran focused builds.

27
00:02:13,087 --> 00:02:15,336
Git carried the auditable handoff.

28
00:02:15,336 --> 00:02:20,298
Finally, the Lean kernel checked the proof terms exposed by the public API.

29
00:02:21,098 --> 00:02:25,922
Broader mathematical review continues; this project does not replace it.

30
00:02:25,922 --> 00:02:30,010
Lean verifies the exact formalized formulas and consequences.

31
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:36,576
It does not certify historical priority, publication status, peer review, or community acceptance.

32
00:02:36,576 --> 00:02:40,127
The repository records those distinctions explicitly.

33
00:02:40,927 --> 00:02:47,080
Breaking Math Verification turns a fast-moving claim into a reproducible first verification layer.

34
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:52,229
The source is traceable, the witnesses explicit, and the trust boundary auditable.

35
00:02:52,229 --> 00:02:53,862
Do not trust the headline.

36
00:02:53,862 --> 00:02:55,306
Verify the certificate.
